  <div id="watermark-tr">
arXiv:2606.13565v1 [cs.LG] 11 Jun 2026</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line" lang="en">
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p">1]Department of Computer and Information Science, University of Pennsylvania
2]School of Mathematics, Georgia Institute of Technology
3]Department of Bioengineering, University of Pennsylvania</p>
</div>
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete 
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:8.5pt;"> Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Sophia Tang
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Yuchen Zhu
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Molei Tao
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Pranam Chatterjee
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>[
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>[
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>[
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Discrete diffusion models offer a simple and stable likelihood-based framework for sequence generation, recently extended to any-length settings via token insertion. Principled reward-guided fine-tuning for any-length discrete diffusion, however, remains largely unexplored. We introduce Fine-Tuning <span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>ny-Length <span id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iscrete <span id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iffusion for <span id="abstract1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>daptive Decoding (<span id="abstract1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2D2</span>), a unified framework for reward-guided fine-tuning of any-length discrete diffusion models via joint optimization of the insertion and unmasking policies together with a quality-based inference schedule. We derive the Radon–Nikodym derivative for the joint insertion–unmasking path measures, enabling theoretically guaranteed convergence to the intractable reward-tilted sequence distribution without requiring target samples. Building on this, we establish unmasking and insertion quality as tractable approaches for minimizing decoding error and introduce the <span id="abstract1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Joint Decoding (AJD)</span> loss, which provably yields the optimal path measure that generates the reward-tilted distribution. Empirically, A2D2 improves reward optimization while enhancing generation flexibility and accuracy over prior fixed-length fine-tuning and inference-time guidance methods.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">Correspondance: <a href="mailto:sophtang@seas.upenn.edu" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_medium">sophtang@seas.upenn.edu</a></span>, <a href="mailto:pranam@upenn.edu" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href ltx_font_typewriter">pranam@upenn.edu</a></p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discrete diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>)</cite> have emerged as a leading paradigm for sequence generation, overcoming key limitations of autoregressive models through bidirectional context, any-order generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, flexible reward guidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nisonoff et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, and parallel decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christopher et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. These properties have driven strong performance across biological sequence design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025c</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gruver et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, and efficient sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Holderrieth et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Among these approaches, <span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">masked discrete diffusion models</span> (MDMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite> stand out for their simple design and stable likelihood-based objective, and have recently been extended to any-length generation by allowing masked-token insertion at arbitrary positions during the diffusion process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. However, scaling any-length discrete diffusion to reward optimization and fine-tuning remains largely unexplored.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">While principled approaches have been introduced for reward fine-tuning fixed-length discrete diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zekri and Boullé, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, any-length MDMs introduce a substantially larger action space that spans both unmasking and variable-length insertions, making performance highly sensitive to the chosen trajectory. This motivates our <span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">key question</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Can we efficiently fine-tune any-length discrete diffusion models to sample from an intractable reward-tilted distribution while preserving high generation quality?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To answer this, we introduce Fine-Tuning <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>ny-Length <span id="S1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iscrete <span id="S1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iffusion for <span id="S1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>daptive Decoding (<span id="S1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2D2</span>), a unified framework for reward-guided fine-tuning of any-length discrete diffusion models via joint optimization of the insertion and unmasking policies and quality-based inference schedule.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.13565v1/Figures/a2d2.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/201;" width="429" height="201" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding.<span id="S1.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A2D2 jointly fine-tunes the insertion and unmasking policies together with a quality classifier to sample from the optimal reward-tilted distribution <math id="S1.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Sequences are generated via adaptive inference and stored in a replay buffer, then used to compute the Adaptive Joint Decoding loss <math id="S1.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AJD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which weights each sequence’s contribution by an importance weight <math id="S1.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo mathsize="1.580em">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="1.580em">¯</mo></mover></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our <span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">main contributions</span> can be summarized in the following points:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the Radon-Nikodym derivative for the joint insertion and unmasking path measures, which enables theoretically guaranteed convergence to an intractable reward-tilted sequence distribution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish unmasking and insertion quality as tractable methods of minimizing compounding parallelization error (CPE) and introduce the <span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Joint Decoding (AJD)</span> loss, which provably yields the optimal path measure that <span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">minimizes error</span> and <span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">generates the reward-tilted distribution</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We demonstrate that A2D2 simultaneously optimizes rewards while enhancing generation flexibility and accuracy over prior fixed-length fine-tuning and inference-time guidance approaches.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Related Works</h4>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A discussion of additional related works is provided in App <a href="#S7" title="7 Related Work ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Masked Discrete Diffusion Models</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The discrete diffusion paradigm models sequence generation as a continuous-time Markov chain (CTMC), which starts at an uninformative prior distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{prior}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{prior}}</annotation></semantics></math> and makes discrete jumps over a finite time horizon <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to generate a sample from the data distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Masked discrete diffusion models</span> (MDMs) have a unique prior distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{prior}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{prior}}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of fully masked sequences <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{M})^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{M})^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Given a clean data distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MDM’s forward process progressively converts clean tokens to masked tokens according to a schedule. Then, the training process aims to reconstruct the clean sequence <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> from intermediate partially masked sequences <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">denoising cross-entropy (DCE)</span> loss:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{DCE}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DCE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{DCE}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}:[0,1]\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}:[0,1]\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the unmasking schedule bounded by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that a given token is unmasked at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in the forward masking process and the unmasking occurs in the reverse process if the time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than the unmasking time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}dt</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{u}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{u}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the standard linear schedule, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Any-Length Discrete Diffusion</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To overcome fixed-length initialization, any-length discrete diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">insert</span> tokens along the generation process. We build on the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">flexible-length masked diffusion model</span> framework of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, which defines a <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">joint stochastic interpolant</span> over insertion and unmasking.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The forward corruption process gradually masks <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span> removes tokens by drawing an insertion time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math> and unmasking time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\bm{1}[t\geq t^{\ell}_{i}]\frac{\dot{\beta}t}{1-\beta{t_{i}^{\ell}}}\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\bm{1}[t\geq t^{\ell}_{i}]\frac{\dot{\beta}t}{1-\beta{t_{i}^{\ell}}}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>, enforcing that a token is unmasked only after insertion (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\ell}_{u}&gt;t_{i}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\ell}_{u}&gt;t_{i}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>). We track the position of each clean token via <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the index in <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>th token in <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}</annotation></semantics></math>. We parameterize both an <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unmasking posterior</span> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\Delta^{V-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\Delta^{V-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and an <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">insertion expectation</span> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the predicted number of tokens to insert at each gap, and minimize:
<span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">insert</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})}\phi\left(s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1,g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.630em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.630em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})}\phi\left(s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1,g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\bigg[-\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.630em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.630em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\bigg[-\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x,y)=y-x\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x,y)=y-x\log y</annotation></semantics></math> is the scalar Bregman divergence. A detailed background on any-length MDMs is provided in App <a href="#S8.SS2" title="8.2 Any-Length Masked Diffusion ‣ 8 Extended Theoretical Background ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first introduce <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unmasking quality</span> and relate it to the error accumulated in a single unmasking step (Sec <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), then derive an analogous, theoretically grounded notion of <span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">insertion quality</span> (Sec <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Unmasking Quality</h3>

<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Defining Unmasking Quality</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unmasking quality</span> as the probability that the unmasked token is sampled from the unmasking posterior given the context from the rest of the sequence. Concretely, given a clean sequence from the target <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a sample along the interpolant <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, a masked position <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, a set of masked tokens <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that are unmasked to obtain <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the unmasking posterior at position <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})=f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})=f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the unmasking quality as:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})=f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}^{\ell}_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})=f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}^{\ell}_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which aligns with the definition of the <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">per-token quality</span> introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. When the probability of the true token <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\ell}=\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is high given the unmasked context <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\text{UM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mtext>UM</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\text{UM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the quality is high, and if the probability is low, then the quality is low. To predict the quality of an already unmasked token <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> such that it estimates the unmasking posterior defined on its masked state <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}\leftarrow\bm{M}}=\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}\leftarrow\bm{M}}=\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we train a parameterized model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}:\mathcal{X}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}:\mathcal{X}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> given its unmasked state <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\approx p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\approx p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">During inference, when we do not have access to the ground-truth sequence <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unmasking quality determines which tokens are inconsistent and should be re-masked.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To train <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}:\mathcal{X}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}:\mathcal{X}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we start with a clean sequence from the target distribution <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> and sample an intermediate state from the joint interpolant <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by partially masking and removing tokens in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we take a single unmasking step to obtain <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing a subset <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> of tokens in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with the clean token sampled from the unmasking posterior <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we minimize an <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unmasking Quality Loss</span> (UQL) defined as:
<span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1}),\bm{y}}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{M}}\text{BCE}\left(\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}],\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.630em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.630em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo><mo mathsize="0.630em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒚</mi></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.630em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mtext mathsize="0.900em">BCE</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟏</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1}),\bm{y}}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{M}}\text{BCE}\left(\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}],\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where BCE denotes the <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">binary cross-entropy</span> loss defined as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unique minimizer</span> of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the unmasking quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unique Minimizer of Unmasking Quality Loss)<span id="S3.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The unique minimizer of the unmasking quality loss <math id="S3.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the true unmasking quality:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\star}=\mu_{\phi^{\star}},\quad\text{where}\quad\phi^{\star}=\underset{\phi}{\arg\min}\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="italic">ϕ</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\star}=\mu_{\phi^{\star}},\quad\text{where}\quad\phi^{\star}=\underset{\phi}{\arg\min}\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is stated in App <a href="#S9.SS2" title="9.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.2</span></a>. We note that this coincides with the loss defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025b)</a></cite> for parameterizing the unmasking quality of fixed-length MDMs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compounding Parallelization Error of Unmasking Steps</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unmasking</span>, the compounding parallelization error is the KL divergence between the true joint distribution over tokens unmasked in a step and the product of their marginals <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, defined as the gap between sequential single-token unmasking and the factorized approximation made when unmasking in parallel.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unmasking Compounding Parallelization Error)<span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a unmasking step from state <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> tokens unmasked in parallel at time <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The unmasking CPE over the transition <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\to t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\to t</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmsk}}(s\to t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CPE</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">unmsk</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmsk}}(s\to t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{K}}|\bm{x}_{s})\bigg\|\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{K}}|\bm{x}_{s})\bigg\|\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the marginal distribution of sequences at time <math id="S3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimal Parallel Unmasking as Maximizing the Unmasking Quality</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that unmasking quality provides an upper bound for the probability of successful parallel unmasking.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Relationship Between Unmasking Quality and Parallel Unmasking)<span id="S3.Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that in a parallel unmasking step on indices <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unmasked tokens are conditionally independent given the unchanged context <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and the current state <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>. If we define the unmasking quality <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t}):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t}):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> and note that <math id="S3.Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is deferred to App <a href="#S9.SS4" title="9.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.4</span></a>. This establishes the theoretical grounding for our adaptive unmasking strategy, which remasks low-quality tokens in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure only mutually high-quality tokens are unmasked in parallel, which effectively maximizes the probability of optimal parallel unmasking.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Insertion Quality</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Defining Insertion Quality</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is natural to define the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">insertion quality</span> as the probability that the insertion is likely to be decoded into a true token in the corresponding gap of the target sequence. Concretely, given a clean sequence from the target distribution <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a sample along the interpolant <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define quality of a mask inserted between positions <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}:=\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>:=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}:=\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as:
<span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\underset{s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]}{\max}\left\{p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.630em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.630em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.630em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\underset{s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]}{\max}\left\{p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which returns the highest probability of any ground truth token between positions <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell-1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> in the clean sequence <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> being predicted by the unmasking posterior <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\bm{y}^{i}=\cdot|\bm{y})=f_{\theta}(\bm{y},t)[i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y}^{i}=\cdot|\bm{y})=f_{\theta}(\bm{y},t)[i]</annotation></semantics></math> at the newly inserted mask token <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}^{i}=(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}})^{i}=\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{i}=(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}})^{i}=\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Alternatively, we can define the set of tokens <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\ell}:=\{\bm{x}^{i}_{1}:s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\ell}:=\{\bm{x}^{i}_{1}:s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]\}</annotation></semantics></math> in the gap between positions <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and the insertion quality as the sum of the probabilities of the tokens in <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, given by:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu^{\ell}_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\sum_{\bm{v}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}}p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{v}|\bm{y})=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}|\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu^{\ell}_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\sum_{\bm{v}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}}p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{v}|\bm{y})=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}|\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is high when several potential tokens have a <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">high potential</span> to be unmasked to one of the tokens within the gap. Note that when there is <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">no token</span> between positions <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell-1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quality is zero. Since we have no access to the ground truth sequence at inference, we aim to train a parameterized model <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> that takes only the sequence <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">after the insertion step</span> <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> as input and approximates the quality of the insertion:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu^{i}_{\phi}(\bm{y})\approx\sum_{\bm{v}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}}p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu^{i}_{\phi}(\bm{y})\approx\sum_{\bm{v}\in\mathcal{S}_{\ell}}p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This allows us to evaluate the quality of an insertion and remove low-quality insertions that are likely to result in mistakes in unmasking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training the Insertion Quality Predictor</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To train <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{\ell}_{\star}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{\ell}_{\star}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, we start with a clean target sequence <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply the standard joint interpolant to sample <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by partially masking and removing tokens in <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we insert the set of masks <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\{\bm{y}^{i}\;|\;\bm{x}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}};g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\{\bm{y}^{i}\;|\;\bm{x}_{t}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}};g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\}</annotation></semantics></math> predicted by the insertion expectation <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> at each gap to get <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and predict the unmasking posterior over the newly inserted masked positions <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{y},t)[i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{y},t)[i]</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we minimize the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Insertion Quality Loss</span> (IQL), defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{y}\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒚</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{y}\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where BCE denotes the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bernoulli cross-entropy</span> loss for two values in defined as <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c)</annotation></semantics></math> for two values <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. If there are multiple masks <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y}^{i_{1}},\dots,\bm{y}^{i_{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y}^{i_{1}},\dots,\bm{y}^{i_{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> inserted in a gap <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell-1]+1},\dots,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell-1]+1},\dots,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, then for each <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sum over the probabilities over the range <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell-1]+d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell-1]+d</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell]-1-(D-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell]-1-(D-d)</annotation></semantics></math>. We show that the minimizer of the insertion quality loss <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the true insertion quality <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Defining Insertion Quality ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) with proof in App <a href="#S9.SS3" title="9.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Minimizer of Insertion Quality Loss)<span id="S3.Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The unique minimizer of the insertion quality loss <math id="S3.Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the true insertion quality:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu_{\star}=\nu_{\phi^{\star}},\quad\text{where}\quad\phi^{\star}=\underset{\phi}{\arg\min}\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="italic">ϕ</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu_{\star}=\nu_{\phi^{\star}},\quad\text{where}\quad\phi^{\star}=\underset{\phi}{\arg\min}\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimizing Reconstruction Likelihood by Maximizing Insertion Quality</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To theoretically justify maximizing insertion quality, we prove that it provides an upper bound for the probability of reconstructing a clean sequence <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Insertion Quality as an Upper Bound on Reconstruction via Insertions)<span id="S3.Thmproposition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a clean target sequence <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> and an intermediate sequence <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}\sim p_{s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}\sim p_{s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a set of indices of inserted masks at each gap <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> which yields <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of reconstructing <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper-bounded by the product of insertion qualities:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{t}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\approx\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{t}}\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{t}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\approx\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{t}}\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the unmasking posterior for each inserted mask is conditionally independent given <math id="S3.Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We defer the proof to App <a href="#S9.SS5" title="9.5 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.5</span></a>. This justifies maximizing insertion quality as optimizing reconstruction quality.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2D2</span>: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce Fine-Tuning <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>ny-Length <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iscrete <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>iffusion for <span id="S4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>daptive Decoding (<span id="S4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2D2</span>), a novel framework tailored for any-length masked diffusion models that jointly optimizes the parameterized quality predictors and policy to sample from the reward-tilted data distribution.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimal Reward-Tilted Path Measure</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> of any-length MDMs consists of both insertion steps <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span> unmasking steps, which form the joint CTMC with rates <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, we aim to define the tilted path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that optimally samples from the reward-tilted distribution <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, we define the tilted path measure as:
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\star}(\bm{X}_{0:1}):=\frac{1}{Z}\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})\exp\left(\frac{r(\bm{X}_{1})}{\alpha}\right),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}(\bm{x})=\frac{1}{Z}p_{\text{data}}(\bm{x})\exp\left(\frac{r(\bm{x})}{\alpha}\right)=:p_{\text{target}}(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">pre</mtext></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">data</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">target</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\star}(\bm{X}_{0:1}):=\frac{1}{Z}\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})\exp\left(\frac{r(\bm{X}_{1})}{\alpha}\right),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}(\bm{x})=\frac{1}{Z}p_{\text{data}}(\bm{x})\exp\left(\frac{r(\bm{x})}{\alpha}\right)=:p_{\text{target}}(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> is a joint CTMC induced by a path measure and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reference path measure induced by the pre-trained insertion rate <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}^{\text{pre}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}^{\text{pre}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and unmasking rate <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\text{pre}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\text{pre}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given parameterized insertion and unmasking rates <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}^{\theta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}^{\theta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\theta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\theta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can optimize <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> such that the path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing the following <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">entropy-regularized reward optimization</span> problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Uehara et al., 2024</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\theta}}\left[r(\bm{X}_{1})\right]-\alpha D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta}\|\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\theta}}\left[r(\bm{X}_{1})\right]-\alpha D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta}\|\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is uniquely minimized when <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta}=\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta}=\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any-length joint CTMCs, the KL-divergence takes a unique form, as derived in App <a href="#S9.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 9.1 (KL Divergence Between Any-Length Joint CTMCs). ‣ 9.7 Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weighted Cross-Entropy Objective</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To derive a loss that provably converges to <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, let’s consider directly minimizing the KL objective <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. While its minimizer indeed matches the optimal measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is difficult to optimize due to the expectation over <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, which changes as the model is updated. Instead, we use the <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">cross-entropy loss</span> which takes the expectation over the <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">fixed</span> target path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star}):=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}\|\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{\star}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star}):=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}\|\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{\star}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the final equality allows us to sample trajectories from any arbitrary path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reweight</span> them such that they approximate the target path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> at the infinite sampling limit. The reweighting term <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Radon-Nikodym derivative (RND) between the two path measures. We derive the full tractable form of the RND in Prop <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Radon-Nikodym Derivative of Parameterized Rates). ‣ Weighted Cross-Entropy Objective ‣ 4.1 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 4 A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radon-Nikodym Derivative of Parameterized Rates)<span id="S4.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the fine-tuned unmasking rate be <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{v}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\Delta^{V-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{v}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\Delta^{V-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the insertion rate be <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{v}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{v}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> that generates the path measure <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, given optimal rates <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\text{pre}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\text{pre}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pre</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> and reward function <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the log RND between the optimal joint CTMC and the fine-tuned CTMC over the trajectory <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:
<span id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\frac{r(\bm{X}_{1})}{\alpha}-\log Z+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{f^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}},t_{u})[\ell,\bm{v}]}{f^{v}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}},t_{u})[\ell,\bm{v}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">pre</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\frac{r(\bm{X}_{1})}{\alpha}-\log Z+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{f^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}},t_{u})[\ell,\bm{v}]}{f^{v}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}},t_{u})[\ell,\bm{v}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}^{\ell}}\log\frac{g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}},t_{i})[\ell]}{g^{v}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}},t_{i})[\ell]}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left(\sum_{\ell}(g^{v}-g^{\text{pre}})(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">pre</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">pre</mtext></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{X}^{\ell}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}^{\ell}}\log\frac{g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}},t_{i})[\ell]}{g^{v}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}},t_{i})[\ell]}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left(\sum_{\ell}(g^{v}-g^{\text{pre}})(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the times of insertion events and <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the times of unmasking events, with <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmproposition1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> being the left limits denoting the pre-jump state in the CTMC.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is given in App <a href="#S9.SS8" title="9.8 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.8</span></a>. Then, defining <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W^{v}(\bm{X}_{1}):=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{v}(\bm{X}_{1}):=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write the cross-entropy loss as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we derive our <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Joint Decoding (AJD)</span> loss, which allows us to optimize the cross-entropy loss without computing the inner RND <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math> over trajectories after each update to the model parameters.</p>
<table id="S4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}[-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}[-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\left[\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}})\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}e^{W^{v}}\left[\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}})\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the first equality follows from dropping the <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> term independent of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second equality follows from decomposing the probability path into the sum of probabilities of each insertion and unmasking step at times <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Rather than explicitly computing the sum over the full trajectory, we observe that each inner term can be reframed as an expectation over samples from the interpolant <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> given a clean sample <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the clean sample <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained by minimizing <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Any-Length Discrete Diffusion ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Any-Length Discrete Diffusion ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Training the Insertion Quality Predictor ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), respectively. This yields our <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Joint Decoding (AJD)</span> loss, defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})+\lambda_{\text{quality}}(\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1}))\big]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AJD</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.710em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">v</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>quality</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})+\lambda_{\text{quality}}(\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1}))\big]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the normalizing constant <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is approximated as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z\approx\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\approx\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}\left[\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. This loss can be seen as an extension of the weighted denoising cross-entropy loss used for fixed-length discrete diffusion sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and fine-tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. This unique minimizer of the AJD loss is the optimal unmasking generator <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion generator <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of the reward-tilted path measure <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, with proof deferred to App <a href="#S9.SS8" title="9.8 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Fine-Tuning Any-Order Discrete Diffusion</h3>

<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Off-Policy Reinforcement Learning</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To optimize the AJD loss, we leverage an <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">off-policy RL</span> strategy with the fixed path measure <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}:=\mathbb{P}^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}:=\mathbb{P}^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by detached parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}:=\texttt{stopgrad}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">stopgrad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}:=\texttt{stopgrad}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\phi}:=\texttt{stopgrad}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">stopgrad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\phi}:=\texttt{stopgrad}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Each fine-tuning iteration: <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> we sample a batch of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> sequences <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> while computing their log RND <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math> and store them in a replay buffer <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\{(\bm{x}_{1,i},W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}})\}_{i=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\{(\bm{x}_{1,i},W^{\bar{\theta},\bar{\phi}})\}_{i=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> for each <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> intermediate sequences from the interpolant <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t,j}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t,j}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1,i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3)</span> we compute the AJD loss (<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 4.1 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 4 A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) and update the parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alternating Optimization of Policy and Quality Predictors</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the number of parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in the insertion and unmasking policy is orders of magnitude larger than the number of parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> in the quality prediction heads, optimizing both models simultaneously results in unstable training and sub-optimal convergence of the quality prediction model. Following prior work, we alternate between updating <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{alt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>alt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{alt}}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> frozen and updating <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{alt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>alt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{alt}}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> frozen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Since the quality heads are initialized from scratch, we sample the replay buffer using only the policy model <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{warmup}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>warmup</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{warmup}}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. Beyond stabilizing training, this alternating schedule acts as an implicit form of loss balancing: because <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are never updated in the same pass, the relative weighting <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{quality}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>quality</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{quality}}</annotation></semantics></math> between the policy losses (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}},\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}},\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the quality losses (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}},\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}},\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}</annotation></semantics></math>) no longer needs to be tuned. Full pseudo-code for fine-tuning with A2D2 is given in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 14 Algorithms ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adaptive Inference with A2D2</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adaptive inference with the unmasking and insertion policy <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta},g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta},g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and quality predictors <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi},\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi},\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> starts from an empty sequence of pad tokens <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and at each discrete time step <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{k},t_{k+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{k},t_{k+1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, performs:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Unmasking</span>: We sample a subset of mask tokens <math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to unmask via the parameterized unmasking posterior <math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we predict the unmasking quality for each token <math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> and re-mask low-quality tokens that either fall below a threshold or until the expected number of masked tokens at time <math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is reached.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Insertion</span>: We insert a set of masks <math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> according by sampling insertion counts <math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\ell}_{t}\sim\text{Poisson}(g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\cdot\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Poisson</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\ell}_{t}\sim\text{Poisson}(g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\cdot\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> for each gap. Then, we predict the insertion quality <math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[i]</annotation></semantics></math> for each inserted mask and subsequently remove low-quality masks.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We stop when no masks remain, and the insertion expectation falls below <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> or when the total number of time steps is reached. The full inference procedure is detailed in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 14 Algorithms ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2D2</span> on two reward-guided sequence generation tasks where any-order, any-length discrete diffusion is particularly well-suited: drug-like small-molecule design (Sec <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Drug-Like Small Molecule Design ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>), multi-objective therapeutic peptide generation (Sec <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Multi-Objective Therapeutic Peptide Generation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>), and language reasoning for math word problems and code infilling (Sec <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Language Reasoning Experiment ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Drug-like small molecule design results.<span id="S5.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Metrics were computed for <math id="S5.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> generated sequences, and the mean and standard deviations were computed across <math id="S5.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> seeds. </span></span></figcaption>
