<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference-Time Scaling of Discrete Diffusion</h4>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Inference-time scaling of diffusion models seeks to maximize the capabilities of pre-trained diffusion models for specialized tasks during inference, such as sampling from a reward-tilted distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Skreta et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Singhal et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, constrained sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fishman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, or entropy maximization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Santi et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Specifically in the discrete state space, search-based methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ramesh and Mardani, 2025</a>)</cite>, importance-weighting techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chatterjee and Diaconis, 2018</a>)</cite>, reward-gradient methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bansal et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and classifier-based and classifier-free guidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nisonoff et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rector-Brooks et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schiff et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rojas et al., 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2024</a>)</cite> have been explored.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training-Time Fine-Tuning of Discrete Diffusion</h4>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training-time fine-tuning methods instead update the model parameters to optimize a downstream reward. One line of work backpropagates rewards through the denoising trajectory, as in DRAKES <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, which makes the otherwise non-differentiable discrete trajectories differentiable via the Gumbel-Softmax trick to optimize sequences that are both high-reward and natural-like. A complementary line adapts policy-gradient reinforcement learning to discrete diffusion: SEPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zekri and Boullé, 2025</a>)</cite> provides a framework that handles non-differentiable rewards via self-normalized importance sampling, while a growing body of work adapts GRPO to masked diffusion language models, including diffu-GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> and Coupled GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. TR2-D2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite> instead casts fine-tuning as stochastic optimal control, using Monte Carlo tree search to curate replay buffers of high-reward trajectories for off-policy RL, and extends to multi-objective reward optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimization of Inference Schedule for Discrete Diffusion</h4>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Closest to our work is PRISM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, which introduces <span id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">per-token quality</span> as a learned measure that determines whether to re-mask already unmasked tokens during inference. However, it remains limited to fixed-length masked diffusion for optimizing sampling of the data distribution. Co-GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which introduces a reward fine-tuning strategy for fixed-length masked diffusion that simultaneously optimizes the inference schedule and policy model with a shared reward signal via group-relative policy optimization (GRPO). Jump Your Steps (JYS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al., 2024</a>)</cite> optimizes the times at which discrete jumps are made during inference by minimizing a KL upper bound on the compounding decoding error for fixed-length masked diffusion models. Related inference-time mechanisms include <span id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">planner</span>-guided decoding, which learns a planner to choose which tokens to reveal at each step <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, as well as remasking and corrector-style methods that iteratively revise intermediate predictions to improve sample quality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Extended Theoretical Background</h2>

<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1 </span>Notation</h3>

<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the CTMC of a diffusion trajectory as <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}:=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}:=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> which lies in the variable-length discrete state space <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\bigcup_{l}\mathcal{V}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\bigcup_{l}\mathcal{V}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}:=\{1,\dots,V\}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}:=\{1,\dots,V\}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> of sequences of length <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and vocabulary size <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is the variable sequence length and <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum sequence length. An any-length discrete diffusion model is characterized by a path measure <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\in\mathcal{P}(C([0,T];\mathcal{X}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\in\mathcal{P}(C([0,T];\mathcal{X}))</annotation></semantics></math> over trajectories that follow a joint generator <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{t}=\bm{Q}_{t}+\bm{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{t}=\bm{Q}_{t}+\bm{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unmasking rate and <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the insertion rate. Specifically, we denote the pre-trained discrete diffusion model as <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\text{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimal target model as <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a corrupted sequence <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the unmasking posterior is given by <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math> with indices <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\ell,\bm{v}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\ell,\bm{v}]</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the probability of a single token at position <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and the insertion rate is given by <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> with index <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> indicating the insertion expectation between positions <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> of the sequence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2 </span>Any-Length Masked Diffusion</h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we build upon the any-length masked diffusion model framework introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, which leverages a pair of joint stochastic interpolants for the insertion and unmasking schedules. Here, we will provide a comprehensive background on the any-length MDM framework and highlight its distinction from standard fixed-length MDMs.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forward Noising Process</h4>

<div id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In standard MDM, the forward process involves applying mask tokens gradually across the sequence until the sequence is fully masked at time <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For any-length MDMs, the forward process consists not only of the masking step but also of a <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">deletion</span> step, which serves as the inverse operation for the insertion step during inference. Therefore, we must define both the insertion time <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and the unmasking time <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for each token position <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S8.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}dt,\quad t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\bm{1}[t\geq t^{\ell}_{i}]\frac{\dot{\beta}}{1-\beta_{t^{\ell}_{i}}}dt,\quad\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\begin{cases}(\text{empty}),&amp;0&lt;t&lt;t^{\ell}_{i}\\
\bm{M},&amp;t^{\ell}_{i}\leq t\leq t^{\ell}_{u}\\
\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]},&amp;t^{\ell}_{u}\leq t\leq 1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>empty</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}^{\ell}\sim\dot{\alpha}_{t}dt,\quad t_{u}^{\ell}\sim\bm{1}[t\geq t^{\ell}_{i}]\frac{\dot{\beta}}{1-\beta_{t^{\ell}_{i}}}dt,\quad\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\begin{cases}(\text{empty}),&amp;0&lt;t&lt;t^{\ell}_{i}\\
\bm{M},&amp;t^{\ell}_{i}\leq t\leq t^{\ell}_{u}\\
\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]},&amp;t^{\ell}_{u}\leq t\leq 1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where (empty) indicates a position that has not been inserted yet. We denote the index of a token in the partial subsequence with <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> given by:</p>
<table id="S8.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{t}:=\{\ell\in\{1,\dots,\text{len}(\bm{x}_{1})\}|\;t^{\ell}_{i}\leq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{t}:=\{\ell\in\{1,\dots,\text{len}(\bm{x}_{1})\}|\;t^{\ell}_{i}\leq t\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> is the index of the token <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{\ell}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{\ell}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and we have <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{len}(s_{t})\leq\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext>len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{len}(s_{t})\leq\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parameterization</h4>

<div id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Just like fixed-length MDMs, the masking step in any-length MDMs has an inverse unmasking step that is parameterized with an <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unmasking posterior</span> <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]:\mathcal{V}^{L}\times[0,1]\to\Delta^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]:\mathcal{V}^{L}\times[0,1]\to\Delta^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> that predicts the distribution over the token vocabulary for each masked position. This model is trained with the standard denoising cross-entropy loss defined as:</p>
<table id="S8.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\bigg[-\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\bigg[-\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\sum_{\ell:\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}=\bm{M}}\log f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell,\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since any-length MDMs contain the additional deletion step, we parameterize the inverse <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">insertion</span> step with a <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">insertion expectation</span> <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]:\mathcal{V}^{L}\times[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]:\mathcal{V}^{L}\times[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> which predicts the number of tokens that still need to be inserted between tokens <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{\ell-1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{\ell-1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{\ell}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This model is trained by minimizing the scalar <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bregman divergence</span> <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x,y)=y-x\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x,y)=y-x\log y</annotation></semantics></math> between the predicted insertions and the true number of tokens that need to be inserted at each position:</p>
<table id="S8.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})}\phi\left(s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1,g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\bm{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{\text{len}(\bm{x}_{t})}\phi\left(s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1,g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Minimizing both losses <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> yields the <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unique</span> optimal value, which defines the rate matrices of the reverse process given by:
<span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⊲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑴</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\triangleleft_{\ell}\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\cdot\mathbb{E}[s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1|\;\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x}]=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\cdot g_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\cdot\mathbb{E}[s_{t}[\ell]-s_{t}[\ell-1]-1|\;\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x}]=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\cdot g_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Insertion Rate)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{v}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{v}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\cdot\mathbb{P}(\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}=\bm{v}|\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x})=\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\cdot f_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)[\ell,\bm{v}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒗</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\cdot\mathbb{P}(\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}=\bm{v}|\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x})=\frac{\dot{\beta}_{t}}{1-\beta_{t}}\cdot f_{\theta}(\bm{x},t)[\ell,\bm{v}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Unmasking Rate)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adaptive Sampling Guarantee</h4>

<div id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">crucial feature</span> of any-length MDMs is that the values of the rate matrix are <span id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">decoupled from the choice of masking schedule <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. This means that the unmasking posterior learned by <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion expectation <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> capture all possible unmasking transitions that interpolate between the empty prior <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the target distribution <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given this, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025a)</a></cite> proves that any adaptive any-length MDM sampler for the <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> will generate a sequence of intermediate states <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{x}_{t_{i}}\}_{i=1}^{N_{\text{steps}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>steps</mtext></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{x}_{t_{i}}\}_{i=1}^{N_{\text{steps}}}</annotation></semantics></math> where the final sequence <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sample from <math id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<section id="S9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.1 </span>Observations</h3>

<div id="S9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout the theoretical proofs, we make the following <span id="S9.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">key observations</span>:</p>
<ol id="S9.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S9.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unmasking rate <math id="S9.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion rate <math id="S9.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> do not overlap, such that:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0,\quad\forall t,\bm{x},\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0,\quad\forall t,\bm{x},\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which follows from the fact that insertion and unmasking actions are disjoint.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total generator <math id="S9.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposes additively:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{A}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\forall t,\bm{x},\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{A}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\forall t,\bm{x},\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both insertion and unmasking rates are <span id="S9.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">valid</span> such that:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x})=-\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x})=-\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x})=-\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{x})=-\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}),\quad\sum_{y\neq x}\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.I1.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which ensures that the CTMC is well-defined such that reward tilting preserves the generator structure.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The tilted generators <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\star}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\star}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and the reference generators <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{0}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{0}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same support, such that:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Q}^{0}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0\implies\bm{Q}^{\star}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Q}^{0}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0\implies\bm{Q}^{\star}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{R}^{0}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0\implies\bm{R}^{\star}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{R}^{0}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0\implies\bm{R}^{\star}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which ensures that the path measures <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.I1.ix4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> are mutually absolutely continuous.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 3.1 (Unique Minimizer of Unmasking Quality Loss). ‣ Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="S9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S9.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="37.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 37.46" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,37.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EAE9FF;" fill="#EAE9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.68 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="637.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S9.SS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.07em;">
<span id="S9.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 3.1 (Unique Minimizer of Unmasking Quality Loss). ‣ Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall the <span id="S9.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unmasking Quality Loss</span> <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1}),\bm{y}}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{M}}\text{BCE}\left(\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}],\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒚</mi></mrow></munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mtext>BCE</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{x}_{1}):=\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1}),\bm{y}}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\sim p_{s|t}(\cdot|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{M}}\text{BCE}\left(\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}],\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Given a clean sequence <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sample from the posterior <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we sample a subset <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of masked indices in <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to unmask to obtain <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample <math id="S9.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\ell}\sim f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a position <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the random binary variable <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by categorically sampling from <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},t)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math> and the model predicted token quality <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle b^{\ell}:=\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\in\{0,1\},\quad c_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{\ell}:=\bm{1}[\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}]\in\{0,1\},\quad c_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For every position <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we minimize the following loss:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\ell):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\left(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\ell):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\left(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Applying the law of total expectation, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\left(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}\underbrace{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\big[\text{BCE}(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y}))\big|\bm{y}\big]\right]}_{:=D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\left(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y})\right)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}\underbrace{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\big[\text{BCE}(b_{\ell},c_{\ell}(\bm{y}))\big|\bm{y}\big]\right]}_{:=D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Let us define the conditional random variable:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(b_{\ell}=1|\bm{y})=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left[b_{\ell}|\bm{y}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(b_{\ell}=1|\bm{y})=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left[b_{\ell}|\bm{y}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Then, we can write the BCE loss <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c)</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})\log c_{\ell}-(1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y}))\log(1-c_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})\log c_{\ell}-(1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y}))\log(1-c_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Differentiating with respect to the parameters <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> denoted as <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and setting the derivative equal to <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that the minimizer is:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dc_{\ell}}D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=-\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c_{\ell}}+\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{1-c_{\ell}}\implies\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c^{\star}_{\ell}}=\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{1-c^{\star}_{\ell}}\implies c_{\ell}^{\star}=q_{\ell}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dc_{\ell}}D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=-\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c_{\ell}}+\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{1-c_{\ell}}\implies\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c^{\star}_{\ell}}=\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{1-c^{\star}_{\ell}}\implies c_{\ell}^{\star}=q_{\ell}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Taking the second derivative with respect to <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that this minimizer is unique:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dc_{\ell}^{2}}D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c_{\ell}^{2}}+\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{(1-c_{\ell})^{2}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dc_{\ell}^{2}}D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})=\frac{q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{c_{\ell}^{2}}+\frac{1-q_{\ell}(\bm{y})}{(1-c_{\ell})^{2}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p">Since we defined the true unmasking quality as <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y}):=p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{s_{t}[\ell]}|\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly matches the true unmasking posterior:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{\ell}^{\star}=q_{\ell}(\bm{y})=\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y})=\underset{c_{\ell}\in[0,1]}{\arg\min}\left\{D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{\ell}^{\star}=q_{\ell}(\bm{y})=\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y})=\underset{c_{\ell}\in[0,1]}{\arg\min}\left\{D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.9" class="ltx_p">Since for all pairs <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have shown that the BCE loss <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized at <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})=\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}^{\ell}(\bm{y})=\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, so the function that minimizes the full objective <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}[D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}[D_{\ell}(\bm{y},c_{\ell})]</annotation></semantics></math> must be the true function <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="S9.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.3 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Minimizer of Insertion Quality Loss). ‣ Training the Insertion Quality Predictor ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="S9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S9.SS3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="37.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 37.46" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,37.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EAE9FF;" fill="#EAE9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.68 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="637.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S9.SS3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.07em;">
<span id="S9.SS3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS3.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Minimizer of Insertion Quality Loss). ‣ Training the Insertion Quality Predictor ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall the <span id="S9.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Insertion Quality Loss</span> <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Training the Insertion Quality Predictor ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the BCE is defined as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c),\quad b,c\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{BCE}(b,c)=-b\log c-(1-b)\log(1-c),\quad b,c\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since the sum <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is inside the expectation, and the loss is calculated independently for each position <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, minimizing <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing the following for every inserted position <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;i):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;i):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Applying the law of total expectation, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{y}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E44.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}\underbrace{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\big|\bm{y}\right]\right]}_{:=B_{i}(\bm{y},c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>BCE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}\underbrace{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{1},\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left[\text{BCE}\big(\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y}),\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\big)\big|\bm{y}\right]\right]}_{:=B_{i}(\bm{y},c)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where we define <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}:=\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}:=\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> as the scalar predicted insertion quality at position <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> as the prediction error given the input sequence <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and predicted quality <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it suffices to prove that for all <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},i)</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction error is <span id="S9.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">uniquely minimized</span> at <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fixing a pair <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},i)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{i}:=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1],\quad c_{i}:=\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{i}:=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1],\quad c_{i}:=\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which yields the prediction error objective:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=-b_{i}\log c_{i}-(1-b_{i})\log(1-c_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=-b_{i}\log c_{i}-(1-b_{i})\log(1-c_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Differentiating with respect to <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (parameterized model), we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dc_{i}}B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=-\frac{b_{i}}{c_{i}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dc_{i}}B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=-\frac{b_{i}}{c_{i}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and setting the derivative to zero, we get the minimizer:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{b_{i}}{c^{\star}_{i}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c^{\star}_{i}}=0\implies\frac{b_{i}}{c^{\star}_{i}}=\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c^{\star}_{i}}\implies c^{\star}_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{b_{i}}{c^{\star}_{i}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c^{\star}_{i}}=0\implies\frac{b_{i}}{c^{\star}_{i}}=\frac{1-b_{i}}{1-c^{\star}_{i}}\implies c^{\star}_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">To prove uniqueness, we take the second derivative:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dc_{i}^{2}}B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=\frac{b_{i}}{c_{i}^{2}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{(1-c_{i})^{2}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dc_{i}^{2}}B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})=\frac{b_{i}}{c_{i}^{2}}+\frac{1-b_{i}}{(1-c_{i})^{2}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">So, the objective function is convex in <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the minimizer is unique. Therefore, we conclude that:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{i}=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})=\underset{c_{i}\in[0,1]}{\arg\min}\left\{B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{i}=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})=\underset{c_{i}\in[0,1]}{\arg\min}\left\{B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS3.p3.7" class="ltx_p">We have shown that for all <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},i)</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction error is uniquely minimized at <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}^{i}(\bm{y})=\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, the only function <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the outer expectation <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}[B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{y}}[B_{i}(\bm{y},c_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math> is the true function <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="S9.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Relationship Between Unmasking Quality and Parallel Unmasking). ‣ Optimal Parallel Unmasking as Maximizing the Unmasking Quality ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="S9.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 9.1</span></span><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal Parallel Unmasking as Maximizing the Unmasking Quality)<span id="S9.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that in a parallel unmasking step on indices <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unmasked tokens are conditionally independent given the unchanged context <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and the current state <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.
<math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
If we define the unmasking quality <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t}):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t}):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> and note that <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, the compounding parallelization error can be written as the KL divergence</span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathrm{CPE}}_{\mathrm{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s}):=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\,\middle\|\,\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\right)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>unmask</mi><mi>CPE</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathrm{CPE}}_{\mathrm{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s}):=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\,\middle\|\,\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\right)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and admits the decomposition</span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathrm{CPE}}_{\mathrm{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\big[\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\big]-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\big[\log\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>unmask</mi><mi>CPE</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathrm{CPE}}_{\mathrm{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\big[\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\big]-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\big[\log\mu_{\star}^{\ell_{k}}(\bm{x}_{t})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with equality to <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if the KL divergence is <math id="S9.Thmproposition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., optimal parallel decoding).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall the definition of token quality. Given a partially masked and deleted sequence <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unmasking quality of each token <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that given the sequence masked at position <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> via the unmasking posterior <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s},s)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is written as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(\tilde{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell\leftarrow\bm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consider a unmasking step <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}\to\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}\to\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> where a subset of <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> tokens with indices <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}:=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}:=\{\ell_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are unmasked where <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of the sequence that remains unchanged from <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\to t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\to t</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the joint conditional and the product of marginals conditioned on <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> be denoted as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}(\cdot):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s}),\quad q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}(\cdot):=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}(\cdot):=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s}),\quad q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}(\cdot):=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, the compounding parallelization error (CPE) of the step is given by:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=D_{\text{KL}}\left(p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\|q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\right)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext><mtext>CPE</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=D_{\text{KL}}\left(p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\|q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\right)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext><mtext>CPE</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})=0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}=q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}=q_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and all the unmasked tokens are <span id="S9.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">conditionally independent</span> such that the product of the marginal probabilities and the joint probability is equal given <math id="S9.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding the KL divergence yields:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext><mtext>CPE</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\sim p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}}\left[\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\right]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}\sim p_{\mathcal{M}_{t}}}\left[\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})\right]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the case where all unmasked tokens are conditionally independent, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In addition, under conditional independence of <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of a particular unmasked token <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> should be the same given the context <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and given the context with only <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> masked <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which aligns with the definition of the true unmasking quality. Therefore,</p>
<table id="S9.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})=:\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}}|\bm{x}_{t}^{\ell_{k}\leftarrow\bm{M}})=:\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#S9.E59" title="Equation 59 ‣ 9.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) into the optimal parallel unmasking condition in (<a href="#S9.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ 9.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mu_{\star}^{\ell}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which means that maximizing the product of token qualities maximizes the probability of optimal parallel unmasking. We can also derive a tractable Monte Carlo estimator for the CPE in (<a href="#S9.E57" title="Equation 57 ‣ 9.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) as:
<span id="S9.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathcal{E}}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.900em">CPE</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathcal{E}}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s}),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}=\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\widehat{\mathcal{E}}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}\right]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℳ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℰ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.900em">CPE</mtext></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.900em">CPE</mtext></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{M}_{t}}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s})-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\log p(\bm{x}^{\ell_{k}}_{t}|\bar{\bm{x}}_{s},\bm{x}_{s}),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathcal{E}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}=\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\left[\widehat{\mathcal{E}}^{\text{CPE}}_{\text{unmask}}\right]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">which concludes our proof.  <math id="S9.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.5 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 3.4 (Insertion Quality as an Upper Bound on Reconstruction via Insertions). ‣ Optimizing Reconstruction Likelihood by Maximizing Insertion Quality ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="S9.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S9.SS5.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="37.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 37.46" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,37.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EAE9FF;" fill="#EAE9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 37.46 L 676.77 37.46 L 676.77 0 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.68 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="637.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S9.SS5.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.07em;">
<span id="S9.SS5.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS5.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 3.4 (Insertion Quality as an Upper Bound on Reconstruction via Insertions). ‣ Optimizing Reconstruction Likelihood by Maximizing Insertion Quality ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall the definition of insertion quality as the sum of the probabilities of all possible tokens that exist within the gap in the ground truth sequence, defined as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\underset{s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]}{\max}\left\{p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu_{\star}(\bm{y}):=\underset{s_{t}[\ell-1]&lt;i&lt;s_{t}[\ell]}{\max}\left\{p(\bm{y}^{\ell}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{y})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Consider a target sequence <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>. After an insertion step <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t})\sim g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{s},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t})\sim g_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{s},s)</annotation></semantics></math>, we unmask the masked tokens to reconstruct <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this proof, we assume that the unmasking posterior factorizes across all masked tokens, which gives the equality:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{i}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}p(\bm{x}_{t}^{i}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{i}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\log p(\bm{x}_{t}^{i}=\bm{x}_{1}^{i}|\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since we define the <span id="S9.SS5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">insertion quality</span> <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\star}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\star}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at an inserted mask position <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as the largest probability mass assigned by the unmasking posterior to any of the ground truth tokens at the gap <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{i}:=[s_{t}[i-1],s_{t}[i]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{i}:=[s_{t}[i-1],s_{t}[i]]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\implies\log p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\log\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\implies\log p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\log\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Assuming conditional independence across all inserted masks given <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,we get:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})=\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})=\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}p(\bm{x}^{i}_{t}=\bm{x}^{\mathcal{G}_{i}}_{1}|\bm{x}_{t})\leq\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> means that target tokens are aligned to inserted slots. Taking the expectation over <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t})\sim p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t})\sim p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}\left[p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})\right]\leq\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}\left[\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}\left[p(\bm{x}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}=\bm{x}_{1}^{\mathcal{I}_{t}}|\bm{x}_{t})\right]\leq\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}\left[\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, maximizing <math id="S9.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}\nu_{\star}^{i}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes a tractable upper bound on the probability that all inserted slots are reconstructed correctly, providing a principled surrogate objective for insertion scheduling.  <math id="S9.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.6 </span>Compounding Parallelization Error for Insertion and Unmasking</h3>

<div id="S9.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we establish the following lemma that decomposes the KL divergence between joint distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9.1</span></span><span id="S9.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KL Divergence Chain Rule)<span id="S9.Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The KL divergence between the joint distributions <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{X}_{s},\bm{X}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{X}_{s},\bm{X}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t}(\bm{X}_{s},\bm{X}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t}(\bm{X}_{s},\bm{X}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> on the joint space <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite discrete state space, satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{s},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{s},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote marginal distributions and <math id="S9.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{t|s},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{t|s},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote conditional distributions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> By expanding the definition of KL divergence, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s,t}(\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}_{=1}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}+\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}_{=1}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}+\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s}}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}}_{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}_{s})}+\sum_{\bm{x}_{s}}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}}_{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s}}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})}}_{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}_{s})}+\sum_{\bm{x}_{s}}\mathbb{P}_{s}(\bm{x}_{s})\underbrace{\sum_{\bm{x}_{s},\bm{x}_{t}}\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})\log\frac{\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}{\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{s})}}_{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which concludes the proof.  <math id="S9.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 9.2</span></span><span id="S9.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(CPE as Upper Bound on KL Divergence)<span id="S9.Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a sampling schedule <math id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{T\to\dots\to t_{K-1}\to 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T\to\dots\to t_{K-1}\to 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the KL divergence between the sampled distribution <math id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and true distribution <math id="S9.Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded by the total CPE:</span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{1}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\bigg[\mathcal{E}^{\text{ins}}_{\text{CPE}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})+\mathcal{E}^{\text{unmsk}}_{\text{CPE}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CPE</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ins</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CPE</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">unmsk</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\bigg[\mathcal{E}^{\text{ins}}_{\text{CPE}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})+\mathcal{E}^{\text{unmsk}}_{\text{CPE}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall our definition for the CPE for insertion as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}(s\to t):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{X}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg\|p(\mathcal{I}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})p(\bm{X}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}(s\to t):=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\mathcal{I}_{t},\bm{X}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg\|p(\mathcal{I}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})p(\bm{X}_{t}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and the CPE for unmasking as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmsk}}(s\to t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmsk</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmsk}}(s\to t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E72.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{n}}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg\|\prod_{i=1}^{n}p(\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{i}}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\bigg[D_{\text{KL}}\bigg(p(\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{n}}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg\|\prod_{i=1}^{n}p(\bm{X}_{t}^{\ell_{i}}|\bm{X}_{s})\bigg)\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Denoting the joint distribution under the true path measure <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{k+1}|t_{k}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{t_{k}}):=p(\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{n}}|\bm{X}_{t_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{k+1}|t_{k}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{t_{k}}):=p(\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{1}},\dots,\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{n}}|\bm{X}_{t_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the parameterized marginal distribution as <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{k+1}|t_{k}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{t_{k}}):=\prod_{i=1}^{n}p(\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{k+1}|t_{k}}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{t_{k}}):=\prod_{i=1}^{n}p(\bm{X}_{t_{k+1}}^{\ell_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write the terminal distribution generated by both path measures as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{0}=\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K}|t_{K-1}}\dots\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{1}|t_{0}}\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}},\quad\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0}=\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{K}|t_{K-1}}\dots\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{1}|t_{0}}\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{0}=\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K}|t_{K-1}}\dots\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{1}|t_{0}}\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}},\quad\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0}=\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{K}|t_{K-1}}\dots\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{1}|t_{0}}\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Now, using Lemma <a href="#S9.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 9.1 (KL Divergence Chain Rule). ‣ 9.6 Compounding Parallelization Error for Insertion and Unmasking ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.1</span></a>, we can write the KL divergence between the marginals at time <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s,t}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s})\|\mathbb{P}^{\prime}_{t|s}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{s}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>insert</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmask</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{x}_{s}\sim\mathbb{P}_{s}}\left[\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(s\to t|\bm{x}_{s})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(s\to t)+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(s\to t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>insert</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmask</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{s}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{s})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(s\to t)+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(s\to t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where the equality holds if and only if <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s}^{v})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t|s}\|\mathbb{P}_{t|s}^{v})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, applying this inequality over all <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> time steps from <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to\dots\to t_{K-1}\to t_{K}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to\dots\to t_{K-1}\to t_{K}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{0}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{0}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K}}\|\mathbb{P}_{t_{K}}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K}}\|\mathbb{P}_{t_{K}}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K-1}}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{K-1}})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{K-1}\to t_{K})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{K-1}\to t_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>insert</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmask</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{K-1}}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{K-1}})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{K-1}\to t_{K})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{K-1}\to t_{K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center" colspan="2"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}})}_{=0}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\left[\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>insert</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmask</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}}\|\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}})}_{=0}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\left[\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})+\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS6.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Since the distribution at time <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fully empty sequence in any-length MDMs (i.e. <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}}=\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}}=\pi_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}_{t_{0}}=\mathbb{P}^{v}_{t_{0}}=\pi_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>), we have finished the proof. This means that the KL divergence of the generated distribution and the true distribution is zero if and only if the compounding parallelization error over all time steps is zero, i.e. <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>insert</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{insert}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>CPE</mtext><mtext>unmask</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{CPE}}^{\text{unmask}}(t_{k}\to t_{k+1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,\dots,K-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,\dots,K-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="S9.SS6.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.7 </span>Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs</h3>

<div id="S9.Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 9.3</span></span><span id="S9.Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radon-Nikodym Derivative of Joint Any-Length CTMCs)<span id="S9.Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider two joint any-length path measures <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by the unmasking rate matrices <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and the insertion rate matrices <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the Radon-Nikodym derivative over the trajectory <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}=(\bm{X}_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:
<span id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the times of insertion events and <math id="S9.Thmproposition3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{u}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{u}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the times of unmasking events.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> The discrete time log RND between the CTMC path measures <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}=\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}=\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\prime}=\pi_{0}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\prime}=\pi_{0}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are the initial distributions. Now, we have both unmasking and insertion rates given by <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, which denotes the rate of unmasking from state <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\to\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\to\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, which denotes the rate of insertion from state <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\to\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\to\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the total probability of a single jump under the joint path measure <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed into the probability of remaining in the same state (<math id="S9.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}=\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the probability of jumping to a different state (<math id="S9.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\neq\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\neq\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S9.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}=\bm{y}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}}=\bm{x})=\begin{cases}1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})&amp;\bm{y}=\bm{x}\\
\Delta t(\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})&amp;\bm{y}\neq\bm{x}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}=\bm{y}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}}=\bm{x})=\begin{cases}1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})&amp;\bm{y}=\bm{x}\\
\Delta t(\bm{Q}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y})+\bm{R}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{y}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})&amp;\bm{y}\neq\bm{x}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For both cases, we will derive the log ratio of the two CTMCs. When the state remains the same over the interval <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{n},t_{n+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{n},t_{n+1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-ratio expands to:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}{1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}{1-\Delta t\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\big(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\big(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\big)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\big)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},z)\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.4" class="ltx_p">When the state changes over <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{n},t_{n+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{n},t_{n+1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-ratio expands to:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}(\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}|\bm{X}_{t_{n}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\Delta t(\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}{\Delta t(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\Delta t(\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}{\Delta t(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})+\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}}))+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#S9.E79" title="Equation 79 ‣ 9.7 Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>) and (<a href="#S9.E80" title="Equation 80 ‣ 9.7 Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">80</span></a>) into (<a href="#S9.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ 9.7 Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) and taking the limit as <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:
<span id="S9.SS7.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\bigg\{\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" mathsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\bigg\{\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}+\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{Q}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)\bigg\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\Delta t\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t_{n}}}\left(\bm{R}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{n}}(\bm{X}_{t_{n}},\bm{X}_{t_{n+1}})\right)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta t)\bigg\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}-},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS7.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which concludes our proof.  <math id="S9.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S9.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 9.1</span></span><span id="S9.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KL Divergence Between Any-Length Joint CTMCs)<span id="S9.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The KL divergence between two joint CTMCs <math id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P},\mathbb{P}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with unmasking rates <math id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q},\bm{Q}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q},\bm{Q}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion rates <math id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R},\bm{R}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R},\bm{R}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:
<span id="S9.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\bigg[\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\bigg[\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},y)dt\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑹</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}\log\frac{\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}{\bm{R}_{t_{i}}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}},\bm{X}_{t_{i}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{y\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{R}_{t}-\bm{R}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},y)dt\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> The KL divergence is defined as the expectation of the log RND derived in Lemma <a href="#S9.Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 9.3 (Radon-Nikodym Derivative of Joint Any-Length CTMCs). ‣ 9.7 Radon-Nikodym Derivative Between Joint CTMCs ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.3</span></a> as:
<span id="S9.SS7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\prime}\|\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}^{\prime}}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{0}}(\bm{X}_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑸</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{\prime}}\left[\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}\log\frac{\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}{\bm{Q}_{t_{u}}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}-},\bm{X}_{t_{u}})}+\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{z\neq\bm{X}_{t}}(\bm{Q}_{t}-\bm{Q}^{\prime}_{t})(\bm{X}_{t},z)dt\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
