<tbody id="S9.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left(\sum_{\ell}g^{v}(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]-\sum_{\ell}g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">pre</mtext></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left(\sum_{\ell}g^{v}(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]-\sum_{\ell}g^{\text{pre}}(\bm{X}_{t},t)[\ell]\right)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p16.3" class="ltx_p">which concludes our proof.  <math id="S9.SS8.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS8.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS8.p17.1" class="ltx_p">We use this form of the log RND to define the importance weight <math id="S9.SS8.p17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1}):=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1}):=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math> in the AJD loss, which yields the optimal any-length path measure <math id="S9.SS8.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, as we will prove in Prop <a href="#S9.Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 9.4 (Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss). ‣ 9.8 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.4</span></a> below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S9.Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 9.4</span></span><span id="S9.Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss)<span id="S9.Thmproposition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The unique minimizer of the <span id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Joint Decoding (AJD)</span> loss defined as:
<span id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">AJD</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.640em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">v</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">insert</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em">IQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is the optimal unmasking generator <math id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion generator <math id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{R}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{R}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of the reward-tilted path measure <math id="S9.Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS8.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.SS8.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> First, we recall the form of the cross-entropy loss as:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E122.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star}):=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}\|\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{\star}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\text{CE}}(\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi},\mathbb{P}^{\star}):=D_{\text{KL}}(\mathbb{P}^{\star}\|\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{\star}}\left[\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.2" class="ltx_p">Then, we substitute <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed under <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>, minimizing the CE loss is equivlalent to minimizing:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E123.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})}(-\log\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1}))\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})}(-\log\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1}))\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.3" class="ltx_p">Since the path measure <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by disjoint insertion and unmasking decisions, the probability of a path <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{X}_{0:1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{0:1}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as the product of insertion and unmasking rates:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})\prod_{t:\bm{X}_{t^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})\prod_{t:\bm{X}_{t^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})\prod_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}})\prod_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})\prod_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}})\prod_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}}}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.4" class="ltx_p">Taking logs, we have:
<span id="S9.SS8.p18.4.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})+\sum_{t_{i}:\bm{X}_{t_{i}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{i}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\bm{X}_{t_{i}^{-}})+\sum_{t_{u}:\bm{X}_{t_{u}}\neq\bm{X}_{t_{u}-}}-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\bm{X}_{t_{u}^{-}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.5" class="ltx_p">Instead of defining the loss with the probability of generating <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> via only the single trajectory <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define it with the expectation over many possible trajectories by taking an expectation over intermediate samples from the endpoint-conditioned interpolant <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and times <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Then, we have:
<span id="S9.SS8.p18.5.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})+\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\log\mathbb{P}_{\text{insert}}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{X}_{1})-\log\mathbb{P}_{\text{unmask}}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{X}_{1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.630em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.630em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.630em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.630em" minsize="0.630em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">insert</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\mathbb{P}_{0}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0})+\underset{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}{\mathbb{E}}\underset{\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{X}_{1})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[-\log\mathbb{P}_{\text{insert}}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{i}}|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{X}_{1})-\log\mathbb{P}_{\text{unmask}}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{t_{u}}|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t},\bm{X}_{1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.6" class="ltx_p">Since we decompose each step into unmasking via <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and remasking via <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion via <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and deletion under <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the losses as a form of the negative log-likelihood of the step given the <span id="S9.SS8.p18.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ground-truth</span> sequence <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{1}\sim p_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write:</p>
<table id="S9.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E125.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:unmask})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:insert})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:uql})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:iql})}+\text{const}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>unmask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Any-Length Discrete Diffusion ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Any-Length Discrete Diffusion ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>UQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Training the Unmasking Quality Predictor ‣ 3.1 Unmasking Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IQL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Training the Insertion Quality Predictor ‣ 3.2 Insertion Quality ‣ 3 Defining the Unmasking and Insertion Quality ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}(\bm{X}_{0:1})=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:unmask})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:insert})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:uql})}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})}_{(\ref{loss:iql})}+\text{const}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.7" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the minimizer in (<a href="#S9.E123" title="Equation 123 ‣ 9.8 Adaptive Joint Decoding Loss ‣ 9 Theoretical Proofs ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>) is equivalent to:
<span id="S9.SS8.p18.7.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{v}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{P}^{\theta,\phi}}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S9.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E126.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">insert</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">IQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta,\phi}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}^{v}}\bigg[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}(\bm{X}_{0:1})}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.8" class="ltx_p">and defining <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AJD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> as:
<span id="S9.SS8.p18.8.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S9.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S9.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S9.E127.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">AJD</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.630em">𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.640em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.640em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn mathsize="0.640em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.630em">ℙ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.640em">v</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">unmask</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">insert</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">UQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">IQL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑿</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AJD}}(\theta,\phi):=\underset{\bm{X}_{0:1}\sim\mathbb{P}^{v}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\frac{1}{Z}\mathrm{e}^{W^{v}}\big[\mathcal{L}_{\text{unmask}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{insert}}(\theta;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})+\mathcal{L}_{\text{IQL}}(\phi;\bm{X}_{1})\big]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.SS8.p18.9" class="ltx_p">concludes our proof.  <math id="S9.SS8.p18.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10 </span>Small Molecule Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="S10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">10.1 </span>Pre-Training the Any-Length Small-Molecule MDM</h3>

<section id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data</h4>

<div id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We represent molecules using SAFE (Sequential Attachment-based Fragment Embedding) strings using the SAFE tokenizer with a vocabulary size of <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=1880" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1880</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=1880</annotation></semantics></math>, including the special pad (<math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{id}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">id</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{id}=3</annotation></semantics></math>) and mask (<math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{id}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">id</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{id}=4</annotation></semantics></math>) tokens <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Noutahi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. All sequences are tokenized with padding and truncation to a maximum length of <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=256</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The model is pretrained on the SAFE-GPT dataset (<span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">datamol-io/safe-gpt</span>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Noutahi et al., 2024</a>)</cite> hosted on HuggingFace, which contains over 1 billion drug-like molecules sourced from ZINC20 and other chemical databases. The dataset is split into <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="945,455,307" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>945,455,307</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">945,455,307</annotation></semantics></math> training sequences, <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="118,451,032" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>118,451,032</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">118,451,032</annotation></semantics></math> validation sequences, and <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="118,890,444" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>118,890,444</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">118,890,444</annotation></semantics></math> test sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model Architecture</h4>

<div id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The flexible-length model architecture is a 96M-parameter bidirectional transformer based on the Diffusion Transformer (DiT) adapted for discrete masked diffusion over variable-length sequences. The architecture consists of <span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) token embedding layer</span> that projects the vocabulary with <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=1880" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1880</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=1880</annotation></semantics></math> to embeddings of dimension <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=768</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) timestep conditioning</span> that encodes the scalar timestep <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> via sinusoidal positional embeddings (frequency dimension 256), projected through a 2-layer MLP with SiLU activation to a conditioning vector of dimension <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}=128</annotation></semantics></math>, and <span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) Transformer backbone</span> with 12 DiT blocks with Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE, base frequency 10,000) and FlexAttention with block masking for variable-length sequence support. There are two prediction heads: <span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) token prediction head</span> that predicts the unmasking posterior in the form of logits over the vocabulary dimension and <span id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) length prediction head</span> which predicts the per-position expected gap count. The unmasking quality predictor <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and insertion quality predictor <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> are lightweight heads that operate on the final-layer hidden states of the shared backbone, where each applies a LayerNorm followed by a 2-layer MLP (dimensions <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\to d\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\to d\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>) with a GELU activation, producing a per-position scalar that is passed through a sigmoid to yield a quality value in <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hyperparameters are provided in Table <a href="#S10.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Training Details ‣ 10.1 Pre-Training the Any-Length Small-Molecule MDM ‣ 10 Small Molecule Experiment Details ‣ A2D2: Fine-Tuning Any-Length Discrete Diffusion for Adaptive Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Details</h4>

<div id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model is trained for <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="87,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>87,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">87,000</annotation></semantics></math> gradient steps using AdamW with a learning rate of <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and weight decay of 0.03. The learning rate follows a linear warmup over the first 2,000 steps from <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-10}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> followed by cosine annealing to zero over the remaining steps. Training uses a global batch size of <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2,048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,048</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2,048</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented with a per-GPU batch size of 64 across 2 GPUs with 16 gradient accumulation steps. An exponential moving average (EMA) of model parameters is maintained with decay rate <math id="S10.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9999</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S10.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S10.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S10.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters for pre-training any-length peptide and small molecule masked diffusion models.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S10.T4.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:207.0pt;height:107.1pt;vertical-align:-52.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-48.4pt,25.1pt) scale(0.681182051398827,0.681182051398827) ;">
<table id="S10.T4.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S10.T4.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S10.T4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Small Molecule</span></td>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Peptides</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S10.T4.6.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S10.T4.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hidden dimension</span></th>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S10.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">768</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S10.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">768</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S10.T4.6.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S10.T4.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Attention heads</span></th>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S10.T4.6.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S10.T4.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S10.T4.6.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Transformer blocks</span></th>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S10.T4.6.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S10.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
